  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Mobile Detection**\n\nI\'ve been working on a better approach to `useIsMobile`. Initially, I considered setting `setIsMobile` directly within a dependency-free effect, but the Next.js SSR environment makes that tricky because `window` isn\'t always available. Instead, I\'m leaning toward initializing the state more directly, perhaps with a breakpoint constant, to enhance the overall pattern.\n\n\n**Revising the Mobile Check**\n\nI\'ve significantly revised the mobile detection logic. My focus shifted to simplifying the approach within `useEffect`. I\'m now setting the state directly using `window.innerWidth` and a breakpoint constant, to cut down on extraneous code. I\'m focusing on making sure the initial check is handled properly, given that the lint errors pointed out issues with setting state immediately in the `useEffect`. I\'m focusing on ensuring it\'s robust.\n\n\n**Improving Mobile Initialization**\n\nI\'ve refined the initial state handling. Now, I use a direct check of `window.innerWidth` if available, bypassing potential SSR issues. I\'ve also swapped out `window.addEventListener` for `window.matchMedia` and a media query listener. The new approach should be more robust and efficient. I am using a breakpoint constant.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 606663876
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
