  planner_response {
    response: "I have completed the Next.js conversion and interactive expansion for the \"Brands & Beyond \342\200\224 2025\" application, prioritizing a clean, robust component architecture and rich visual feedback using `motion`:\n\n- **Modular Architecture:** Broke down the monolithic HTML structure into reusable logical sections (`Hero`, `Story`, `People`, `Experience`, `Audience`, `Schedule`, and `Packages`), centralizing the layout in `app/page.tsx` for easy maintainability.\n- **Fluid Interactivity & Animation:** \n  - Integrated `motion` to seamlessly power the infinite scrolling photo carousels on the Hero page, allowing them to gently pause dynamically on hover.\n  - Upgraded the static image blocks in the Experience section to use custom 3D tilt interactions that respond to user mouse movement, bringing depth to the layout.\n  - Implemented staggered fade-up effects and parallax scrolling for content elements that emerge organically as you scroll down the page.\n- **Dynamic Metrics:** Replaced the static statistics display with a declarative `AnimatedNumber` hook utilizing Spring physics, which dynamically counts up cleanly as the block enters the viewport.\n- **Tailwind Native Theme Integration:** Abstracted the custom color system (`brand-magenta`, `brand-navy`, `brand-cream`, etc.) and distinct Google Fonts typography pairs (Barlow Condensed & DM Sans) natively into `@theme` for streamlined, utility-first styling across all components. \n\nThe application builds successfully, and all image domains have been configured securely in `next.config.ts`."
    thinking: "**Outlining the Design Concept**\n\nThe build\'s complete! I\'m now outlining the design\'s core concept, explaining the added interactions using `motion` and `Tailwind CSS`. I\'ve structured the HTML into a more logical format.\n\n\n"
