    thinking: "**Analyzing the Layout**\n\nThe compilation is going well! I am now inspecting the `hero.tsx` layout, focusing on the responsive grid structure and the use of `motion.div`. I\'m especially interested in how the `md:` breakpoints are affecting the layout in this component.\n\n\n**Refining the Responsiveness**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the mobile and desktop behavior of the layout, specifically the hero section. I\'ve noted the scaling adjustments and absolute positioning details. The goal is a perfect display across devices. I\'m considering the interplay of `md:w-full` with the positioning, and thinking of ways to improve the visual balance of the background on different viewports.\n\n\n**Adjusting Positioning Details**\n\nI have corrected an issue with the element\'s positioning on the right, which was causing overlap and visibility problems on mobile. Using `top-[15%] right-[-5%]` and changing the parent\'s display to `block` has resolved it. I\'ve also softened the appearance of cards using rounded corners and made the buttons in Hero, Navigation, and Story more rounded.\n\n\n"
