  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Image Loading Issues**\n\nI\'m focusing on why images aren\'t loading, suspecting a misconfiguration in `next.config.ts`. I need to verify the image URLs in `hero.tsx` and `sections.tsx` to confirm if `picsum.photos` and `images.unsplash.com` are correctly handled.\n\n\n**Reviewing Image Configuration**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that Next.js\' `next/image` handles `images.unsplash.com` as expected, particularly when properly configured. It seems `referrerPolicy` is correctly set, but the issue persists. A change in the subdomain of `images.unsplash.com` is possible, but I\'ve verified the URLs, and they\'re consistent. I\'m now investigating potential `next.config.ts` discrepancies, container sizing issues (specifically with zero-height), and the use of the `fill` property without proper relative parent containers in `hero.tsx`.\n\n\n**Implementing Design Refresh**\n\nI\'m now focused on redesigning the hero component and incorporating the requested fonts. I\'ll be implementing `Sora` and `Space Grotesk` fonts by updating `app/layout.tsx` and `app/globals.css`. The previous design of the hero, an infinite scrolling carousel, is being replaced with a cleaner, simpler design to ensure it\'s striking on all devices. I\'m prioritizing beautiful curves and clear imagery for the new hero.\n\n\n**Refining Configuration and Hero**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new hero design, aiming for a cleaner, impactful look across all devices. I\'m swapping the infinite scroll for a simplified hero. I have added `Sora` and `Space Grotesk` fonts by updating `app/layout.tsx` and `app/globals.css`, and modified variables for font use. I\'m focusing on those `referrerPolicy` values on images that are used. I am checking the `next.config.ts`, but it looks correct. The most recent issue may be in the absence of `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` in `sections.tsx`.\n\n\n**Designing Hero Refinements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a cleaner, intuitive hero design. I\'m leaning toward a large, central, rounded image with floating text, and the event name, \"Brands & Beyond 2025,\" and tagline \"Empowering brands for what\'s next.\" The main text will be in `Sora`, soft background, with a stunning hero image below. The styling I am currently focusing on is `rounded-3xl`. Further, I\'ll update sections, ensuring font classes look correct with the new fonts, including mapping `--font-cond` to `Sora` and `--font-sans` to `Space Grotesk`. Finally, I will add `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` to all images in `components/sections.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Font Mapping**\n\nI\'m now refining the font implementation. I\'ve updated `app/layout.tsx` to include both `Space_Grotesk` and `Sora` fonts and their respective CSS variables. I\'m remaping existing font classes within `globals.css` for consistency and clarity: I\'ve updated `--font-sans` to the `Space Grotesk` font, and `--font-cond` to the `Sora` font. I\'ll need to do a bulk edit to update the use of those variables.\n\n\n**Updating Hero Refactor**\n\nI\'m now refactoring the `hero.tsx` component, simplifying the design considerably. I\'m removing the `leftCards` and `rightCards`, and replacing them with a full-height screen with a soft cream background. I am using `Sora` for \"Brands & Beyond 2025\" and integrating a wide, curved image with a parallax effect, and floating text elements. I\'m aiming for a visually striking hero section.\n\n\n**Implementing Parallax Scrolling**\n\nI\'m now integrating a parallax effect into the hero section using `framer-motion`. I\'m using `useScroll` and `useTransform` to create a dynamic visual for a more engaging hero section. I\'m focusing on ensuring the parallax movement feels smooth and visually appealing, using `containerRef` and `scrollYProgress` for positioning and scaling.\n\n\n**Refining Content Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the new content into the hero component. I\'m focusing on the font sizes and ensuring they\'re responsive across different screen sizes, which is important. I\'m also reviewing the text\'s alignment and spacing for optimal readability.\n\n\n**Integrating Hero Section Content**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the content within the refactored hero section. I\'ve integrated a new call to action with a dark navy background and white text. I\'ve implemented a parallax effect for the hero image and am currently concentrating on responsive text and spacing to ensure optimal readability. The image is now a dynamic element, scaling with scroll, and I\'m currently ensuring it displays correctly on all screen sizes.\n\n\n**Implementing UI Component Changes**\n\nI\'m now making component adjustments. Specifically, I am focusing on implementing `referrerPolicy=\"no-referrer\"` for all image components and ensuring appropriate font classes, using a consistent naming scheme. I\'m also reviewing the navbar to improve its responsiveness.\n\n\n**Adapting Navbar Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the new floating pill navbar to ensure it complements the `bg-brand-cream` background of the new hero section. I\'ve re-written the navbar to include the floating pill style. The initial navbar styling will include a `bg-white/80` background, a backdrop blur, and white borders to ensure visibility and modern aesthetics.\n\n\n**Refining App Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the new design elements across the app. I\'m updating the `Header` component, and plan to adjust the `Ticker` and `Footer` to use the new fonts and styles, including mapping `font-cond` to the `font-heading` class for consistency. I am also working to ensure these components remain consistent with the overall branding aesthetic and provide a cohesive user experience.\n\n\n**Refining Content and Variables**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the content and CSS variables. I\'ve switched the font-cond and font-sans classes to the correct fonts via the `globals.css` file. I am looking for ways to streamline and automate these variable updates for future consistency. I\'m also ensuring a uniform application of these stylistic changes across all relevant components.\n\n\n**Adjusting Font Sizes**\n\nI\'m now implementing adjustments to accommodate Sora\'s width. I\'ll strategically modify font sizes in `sections.tsx`, reducing some of the larger sizes to prevent layout overflow. I\'m focusing on text elements that use `text-[clamp(58px,7vw,115px)]`, which may break with `Sora` fonts. I\'m considering using `break-words` as a fallback.\n\n\n**Optimizing Font Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the fonts, confirming Next.js manages them through `next/font/google`. I\'ve verified the `layout.tsx` file\'s correct import of `Space_Grotesk` and `Sora`, complete with proper variable declarations. I\'ve updated the `globals.css` file. Now, I will implement a bulk edit to update variables for consistent use of `Space Grotesk` and `Sora` fonts.\n\n\n**Implementing Hero Changes**\n\nI\'m now rewriting `hero.tsx` and replacing the existing component with a new design. I am also planning on replacing the old SVG file with a simplified image. I\'m focusing on incorporating the parallax effect with `framer-motion`, and ensuring the layout maintains visual impact and responsive design across all devices.\n\n\n\n**Refining Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual elements, focusing on implementing the new hero section. I\'ve successfully incorporated parallax scrolling for an enhanced user experience and I\'m currently working to ensure all content, including text and images, remains responsive and visually appealing across all screen sizes. I\'ve addressed initial layout issues and am working to create the most impactful experience.\n\n\n**Adjusting Component Styles**\n\nI\'m now implementing the adjustments to components. I\'m focusing on the hero section\'s text, specifically, styling the event details with magenta color, font, and size. I\'m now integrating the heading with the correct text size