  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Entrance Animations**\n\nRight now, I\'m focused on understanding the core goal. My primary aim is to implement fading and sliding entrance animations for each section, specifically the `Story`, `People`, and `Experience` components. I\'m leveraging `framer-motion` (or the equivalent import, currently `motion/react`) to achieve this.\n\n\n**Addressing Hero and Animations**\n\nI\'ve tackled the hero image loading issue by checking the URLs in `components/hero.tsx`. I\'m also simplifying the hero section to solve the \"overinformation problem\". Regarding entrance animations, I\'m now wrapping the section components with `motion.section` to apply a fade-up effect on scroll. The elements are defined and used in `components/sections.tsx` with initial states `initial={{ opacity: 0, y: 50 }}` and the view triggers `viewport={{ once: true, margin: \"-100px\" }}`.\n\n\n**Troubleshooting Image Loading**\n\nOkay, so I\'m stuck on why the hero image isn\'t loading, but others are. I\'m investigating why. The `referrerPolicy` seems correct in `HeroColumn`. I\'m revisiting the URLs. Unsplash might be the culprit. I\'m comparing the `components/sections.tsx` and `components/hero.tsx` images. The sections were fixed by the previous step, but the hero was overwritten. Next I\'ll check `next.config.ts` for domain allowance, as well as the need for `unoptimized={true}` or `picsum.photos`.\n\n\n**Resolving Image Sourcing**\n\nI\'ve got it! I realized Unsplash often blocks hotlinking or needs specific referrers, so I\'m updating `next.config.ts` to allow `images.unsplash.com` to guarantee image loading. Alternatively, I could have just used `picsum.photos` which requires no config. I will update to Unsplash for better quality. Also, I\'m working to simplify the hero section by reducing text and making it bolder. I want a minimalistic, sharp design.\n\n\n**Refining Visual Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now streamlining the visual aspects. I\'ve decided to move away from Unsplash and use `picsum.photos` for image sourcing, bypassing `next.config.mjs` configuration. In `components/hero.tsx`, I\'m removing the floating tags and simplifying the main headline to \"Brands & Beyond,\" \"2025,\" and a single CTA. I\'m also simplifying or removing the wave SVGs for a cleaner look. I\'m leaning toward a one or two-column layout.\n\n\n**Implementing Section Animations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on section animations, particularly the fade-in and slide-up effects. I\'ve wrapped the `<section>` elements in `motion.section` within `components/sections.tsx`, applying an initial opacity and vertical offset, with `whileInView` for the animation, as well as timing and easing properties, while also making sure my initial configurations are proper. I\'ll make sure these animations complement the existing `FadeUp` and `RevealHeading` for seamless transitions. Also, I\'m ensuring the section containers themselves have an attractive entrance.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 939603008
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
