    response: "I have resolved the issues and implemented the requested animations:\n\n- **Section Entrance Animations**: I wrapped every major section component (`Story`, `People`, `Experience`, etc.) in a `motion.section` wrapper utilizing `framer-motion`. Now, as you scroll down the page, entire sections elegantly slide up and fade into view, compounding with the internal reveal animations of the individual cards and text.\n- **Hero Decluttering**: I solved the \"overinformation\" problem by aggressively stripping away background noise from the Hero component. The complex wave SVGs, tiny floating timestamp text, and extra subheadings have been removed. The hero now features a bold, sharp, two-column scrolling layout focused entirely on the core typography (\"Brands & Beyond 2025\") and a single registration call-to-action.\n- **Fixed Image Loading**: I replaced the restricted Unsplash image URLs with standard placeholder seeds from `picsum.photos` across both the Hero and Section components. This bypasses the strict cross-origin/referrer blocks caused by the preview iframe, ensuring your imagery loads instantly and reliably on every refresh."
    thinking: "**Fixing Image Loading & Overload**\n\nI\'ve successfully compiled the app! I resolved the image loading issue by swapping out all `images.unsplash.com` URLs for dependable `picsum.photos` URLs in `hero.tsx` and `sections.tsx`. This sidesteps cross-origin blocking within the iframe. I also directly addressed the \"overinformation\" issue in `hero.tsx`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have resolved the issues and implemented the requested animations:\n\n- **Section Entrance Animations**: I wrapped every major section component (`Story`, `People`, `Experience`, etc.) in a `motion.section` wrapper utilizing `framer-motion`. Now, as you scroll down the page, entire sections elegantly slide up and fade into view, compounding with the internal reveal animations of the individual cards and text.\n- **Hero Decluttering**: I solved the \"overinformation\" problem by aggressively stripping away background noise from the Hero component. The complex wave SVGs, tiny floating timestamp text, and extra subheadings have been removed. The hero now features a bold, sharp, two-column scrolling layout focused entirely on the core typography (\"Brands & Beyond 2025\") and a single registration call-to-action.\n- **Fixed Image Loading**: I replaced the restricted Unsplash image URLs with standard placeholder seeds from `picsum.photos` across both the Hero and Section components. This bypasses the strict cross-origin/referrer blocks caused by the preview iframe, ensuring your imagery loads instantly and reliably on every refresh."
