    summary: "The \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" error in a Next.js application typically indicates an attempt to redefine or assign a new value to the `fetch` property on the `window` object, which is read-only in modern browser environments. This error often arises due to the interplay between Next.js\'s server-side rendering (SSR) capabilities and how `fetch` is managed or polyfilled[1][2][3].\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of why this error occurs in Next.js and how to address it:\n\n**Understanding the Error**\n\nThe `fetch` API is a global function on the `window` object in browsers, used for making network requests. In many environments, including modern browsers and Node.js (where Next.js performs SSR), the `window.fetch` property (or its equivalent in Node.js) is implemented as a getter, meaning its value cannot be directly reassigned[2][3]. When a script tries to do `window.fetch = someOtherFetchFunction`, this error is thrown because the property lacks a setter.\n\n**Common Causes in Next.js**\n\n1.  **Server-Side Rendering (SSR) Conflicts:**\n    *   Next.js is an isomorphic framework, meaning your code can run on both the server (Node.js) and the client (browser). The `window` object only exists in the browser. If code that attempts to modify `window.fetch` runs during SSR, it can lead to unexpected behavior or errors, as the `window` object is not available in the Node.js environment[1][4].\n    *   Next.js extends the native `fetch` API for server-side requests, adding features like caching and revalidation. Attempting to override it globally can conflict with Next.js\'s internal mechanisms[5].\n\n2.  **Polyfills and Third-Party Libraries:**\n    *   Some older polyfills (e.g., `whatwg-fetch`) or third-party libraries might attempt to globally replace `window.fetch` when imported. If these run in a context where `fetch` is already defined as a non-configurable getter, it causes the error[6].\n    *   In Node.js environments (used by Next.js for SSR), `fetch` might be polyfilled by libraries like `node-fetch` or Next.js\'s internal `undici`. Conflicts can arise if another library tries to apply its own polyfill or override[1][7].\n\n3.  **Incorrect Fetch Mocking:**\n    *   In testing or development, if you\'re trying to mock the `fetch` API by directly reassigning `window.fetch`, you\'re likely to encounter this error[8]. Safe mocking should involve intercepting requests at a lower network level or using dedicated mocking libraries.\n\n**Solutions and Workarounds**\n\n1.  **Conditional Client-Side Execution:**\n    *   If you need to interact with `window.fetch` or any browser-specific global, ensure your code only runs on the client side. This can be achieved using React\'s `useEffect` hook or by dynamically importing components with `ssr: false`[9][4].\n    \n\nSources:\n[1] [omi.me](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGbK-LckwZ3nSnjujHVvWKG01nJzM0eZ2uKWp6qx1yrS-wFisPZlPYAxkjGVKdDb8eb_V3xZnmx8nkbWHyK7y7jJ6ZaGj6pxTpEBB1XnGwTA5qH-MtCR4vzBO6tH2e8zJa0A4UwBWczMoVE7Kq-qlZdnSDezSBzUVop5Ev0dMPvUw4TOwM32oz2H7DOVx28j89T34i94_rOAzWtg9ePdgtfp1p7T9pYARhsI6d9cKbvHuWGv9tBF8WI6A==)\n[2] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF78OFbmxliQvDYTGIFddzy1-vGshoQA3MpKXNTHz4fwNXrUFXGxXrQoQf3HwT5rQs-OW_5aY3tvIvskL0BFxxrsCfQQ8HUfrZr6R2fPdxK77lrg2Jo3rV2aqklnt06-aCCyy87VU23l0hRWSVYtHft1iAi8MX7rxlpf2KkrFjRPwWsST9T8ScxlEEZddoOZasJNFduKWhao9wXA700PaK46s91tyX4nIdk71zeUnYvTA==)\n[3] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG-i6-_2gGha6TR6AqFkzTnGJu6cx6AS2ObhkkSFfiz_hpE6fKzrh6T-ly13O9cnvQER2mDfmlcKC128fxQA4jge7-sZTAOo9y1wuu7U8GH9VuB0BBFiz-aVDTdXJReZ8iryopn5E2fUcyoZccgW9zRZO2jpoE2kYe0j8hmXrfmgEo1c59dvE2ZHywDYrjfMQRZ_17dH6xmev5ZH_8SfjG_U9Rb0yN25A20-yQMiE48u4Jy)\n[4] [sentry.io](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEuo15SR3EBYit9kfRo0kjZquio9oBlU0QNc0lP4k0CBkT2_wtxNKPNb8XO8Hy7swUfXF1RgpHKIN1sOIu79Hp4a8kFXZw2_KPaW2yFeO9tQWrXPsXASU-Avh_ZfASrhemjpYpObAxoGmGwVA33GCRLz6SB5OlcWpsmesDApK9QYwbHGw==)\n[5] [nextjs.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFJTLgB5SCBFbcPcX9P26iZLlJzG3I1vFczXkcoykxZlEbNYcNHFg-CmgtEe2MlLJp1Wv5YK9hJrWKjYiJSIck0TS4mr2jPL1P1ooc2n259zVlFoVlwZYVWICgWQJXl7cKPIxny5fyrdFJh5ttya_rji5jmSg==)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEtoq2Jtq_ahmu3si3JF82Y9h7StY9DZITvFw1Fski4CxmYXvPHtf44XdABeL02MNhrRsdN4lQYFzqPy9mUCZzdR37VgplCPuLLTpb4tbppTJCP2sQnr0vsHcX_kXr35D4t7LT8iPzM)\n[7] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEcHKowaDkunmhLTwzylVfclkx0QCVLI5xsvI1Xwj9PIm5JIKX7HsvC4kyaVjQjAXKzyNQpHSsFpR_ECoRs5MRLt8OUOrb6hLLxD6o0yRGqofubMzbj-52DJQ1OpcqIjidumd7vU_TqqiSg4-moFohdKNspCPK3--zyyMTYhoOQbf6dxSsU30nwI3s0BWVEGfBeXFh-QdPrwvlTTodnWw==)\n[8] [momentic.ai](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFm3gZWm4LjGaESl4ykkaPG3sdt6FiF8nVhDHjM0j0QArP9yBpnjFY6DplgWcUu03ZH5RO8QPmF-dwkiQm58k0QH4sOwaRxCQOYexjZwTuWrswMjeXVzrXkcm9DN5pSRMNBwB7xbBW5w6zdUH9vlfEV2BkJk0nuvWib)\n[9] [nextjs.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGTmzmoRUPKTK923MW4ri5lfZ5iME2-NJIHVz8jenyxl8EfEkKY1yhBRZImkjMtRr2FogDGm_icwmph7C05AopyI8jeLNHXKlYZdJPr85EYHEZfq-91KJkkaGg9qT3uYN3tt9Wj16uLncY4fQY4h3gwTETzE8VuLiKH5bzqs4GEwc52i05aNE0B2kzoBQ==)\n[10] [openzeppelin.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHI4sMf6S1ORV10kBQNI6bKuFt8Bxy-4ddJ-v6GwIHNBIUhOT-bx6iWAtkA75dUBPI4OV2AjY2P0XEOn7nFqzhg3OC-DE1JTkhOp91_pL_5I3qVoE93ER2duQEfteLmfErJG6fe-AifFDgKSEc45k_3TKRyZKlb_goDMMQCwy_ObC9E3gFABQAuYYrAreNhyM-zfuiuRXQiiUT-0zQacZ5WvyVVRC6ofW6aB-GCCyZBCfjUcNXqz-EGloHLlA==)\n[11] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFFsHDSJjZvg8xSF2ljFj2p7X8LrqsbQfYuF1N6Uo-D3e2SxvLz_4qSBUWhJ5ZwvYV4cl6W2UGNLIMeQtEkahAlM1jahFeVaTVmVKIvihRGtAID-DE7lYDk6x8Y29si