    thinking: "**Identifying the Error Source**\n\nI\'ve hit a snag. The error message, \"TypeError: Cannot set property fetch,\" is staring me in the face. It seems `fetch` can\'t be modified, which is a bit puzzling. Initially, I suspected my code, but now I\'m considering that Next.js might be the culprit. The user recently upgraded to version 15.4.9, which could be relevant. Time to investigate!\n\n\n**Analyzing the `fetch` Conflict**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! The `fetch` issue likely stems from Next.js\'s internal fetch patching. Checking `next/dist/client/app-index.js` and `setup-hydration-warning.js`, it appears Next.js attempts to overwrite `window.fetch`. Because of the way the AI Studio secures iframes, it\'s not writable and throws. I\'m now investigating how to disable Next.js\'s client-side fetch patching or override the getter/setter before Next.js runs, to work around this conflict.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 10121093
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
