    thinking: "**Investigating Fetch Issues**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a potential conflict between Next.js and the `fetch` API. It seems that when a script attempts to override `window.fetch` in the browser, an error arises. This could suggest a clash with a service worker or an instrumentation script injected by Next.js. I\'m going to look closer at the scripts and proxy properties that are created. I need to keep checking the properties of the request itself.\n\n\n**Analyzing Configuration Files**\n\nI\'m now diving into the project\'s configuration files, specifically `next.config.ts`. The contents are mostly standard Next.js setup, including react strict mode, transpile packages (motion), and some webpack configurations. I\'m considering if the environment or a Chrome Extension might be interfering with `window.fetch`. Could the iframe environment within AI Studio be causing the conflict by blocking the modification of `fetch`?\n\n\n"
