  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Implementation**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `whatwg-fetch` implementation, directly injected into Next.js\'s static bundles. It seems a package utilized by Next.js or its dependencies is the culprit. I\'m focusing on the implications of this injection. I\'ll need to dig deeper.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Short Circuit**\n\nI\'ve hit a roadblock. The issue stems from the polyfill attempting to assign `self.fetch=hb` when `self.fetch` is a getter, causing the error. I\'ve been dissecting the `whatwg-fetch` code\'s behavior, particularly the short-circuiting logic in the assignment. Even with a pre-existing `window.fetch`, the `||` operator seems to fail due to how the sandbox environment handles `self.fetch`, likely returning `undefined` from the getter in some cases, or even removing it. I need to understand why the sandbox returns `undefined` and not the native fetch, to better understand why this is happening.\n\n\n**Investigating Patch Options**\n\nI\'m exploring potential patches for the issue. My initial thought is a `<script>` tag interception, or direct manipulation within `app/layout.tsx`, but the `whatwg-fetch` bundle\'s immediate execution makes these options unlikely to work. My current focus is why this error is happening now, and the triggering action was using `unoptimized` on `Image` components and restarting the app, and the user encountered this error. I am currently focused on examining the timing of this error, and how it relates to this.\n\n\n"
