  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating `polyfills.js`**\n\nOkay, I\'m digging into this `polyfills.js` situation. Next.js does serve it for older browsers, that\'s clear. But I\'m now trying to figure out if modern browsers are accidentally executing it too, and why that might be. I\'m hitting a snag though, still trying to understand the undefined `self.fetch` error, since it has a getter, it shouldn\'t be a simple undefined error.\n\n\n**Uncovering Potential Fetch Conflicts**\n\nOkay, I\'m now exploring if another library is mistakenly trying to patch `window.fetch`. I\'m searching the `.next/static/` directory for any instances of `window.fetch =` or `window.fetch=`. The goal is to uncover potential conflicts. This seems to be the current most probable source, since it explains the getter error.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 56614241
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
