  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Polyfills Injection**\n\nI\'ve been examining Next.js\'s polyfill injection, specifically the `<script>` tag with the `nomodule` attribute. The `nomodule=\"\"` attribute is meant to prevent ES module-supporting browsers from running it. Chrome does support ES modules through `<script type=\"module\">`. I need to figure out why the browser is handling this the way it is. This doesn\'t make sense.\n\n\n**Investigating Fetch Assignment**\n\nI\'m now honing in on the fetch assignment issue. I confirmed `whatwg-fetch` only exists in `polyfills.js`, which shouldn\'t be executed in modern Chrome due to `nomodule`. So why the crash? Could the error be from something other than `whatwg-fetch`? I\'m re-evaluating the source of the crash. I\'m now exploring the crash message\'s details.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 739693985
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
